# Click "Send Request" above each block (VS Code REST Client extension or Visual Studio).
@host = http://localhost:5080

### Current standings
GET {{host}}/api/standings

### All players
GET {{host}}/api/players

### Add a player
POST {{host}}/api/players
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Riley" }

### Record a match (Ben won +21, Alex lost -18)
POST {{host}}/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "results": [
    { "playerId": 1, "won": true,  "lpDelta": 21 },
    { "playerId": 2, "won": false, "lpDelta": -18 }
  ]
}

### Invalid match: won with negative LP -> 400 with an error list
POST {{host}}/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "results": [ { "playerId": 1, "won": true, "lpDelta": -20 } ]
}

### One player's LP history with running total
GET {{host}}/api/players/1/history

### Delete a match entered by mistake
DELETE {{host}}/api/matches/1

### ---- Riot API (needs Riot:ApiKey in user-secrets) ----

### Link player 1 to a Riot account (use a real Riot ID)
PUT {{host}}/api/players/1/riot-account
Content-Type: application/json

{ "riotId": "YourName#NA1" }

### Check Riot for new games right now
# The first sync for a player only saves a baseline. Play a ranked game, then sync again.
POST {{host}}/api/sync
